  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\vec{a}, \\vec{b}, \\vec{c}$ are three unit vectors such that $\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}+\\vec{c}=\\overrightarrow{0},$ where $\\overrightarrow{0}$ is null vector, then $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}+\\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{c}+\\vec{c} \\cdot \\vec{a}$ is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "-3",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "-2",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$-\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "0",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have $\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}+\\vec{c}=\\overrightarrow{0}$\r\n\r\n$|\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}+\\vec{c}|=0 \\Rightarrow|\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}+\\vec{c}|^{2}=0$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow|\\vec{a}|^{2}+|\\vec{b}|^{2}+|\\vec{c}|^{2}$\r\n\r\n$+2(\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}+\\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{c}+\\vec{c} \\cdot \\vec{a})=0$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow 1+1+1+2(\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}+\\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{c}+\\vec{c} \\cdot \\vec{a})=0$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}+\\bar{b} \\cdot \\vec{c}+\\bar{c} \\cdot \\bar{a}=-\\frac{3}{2}$"
  }
}